WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.549
Hi I'm Toby and welcome back to another
video. Today I'd like to show you through

00:00:05.549 --> 00:00:11.010
some of the early works of Isaac Newton.
These are very important contributions

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:17.010
to science and mathematics made while
Newton was quarantined at home during

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:24.359
the Great Plague of London. This was a
plague that went from 1665 to 1666, it

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:29.130
was spread by fleas and killed around a
hundred thousand people over the course

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:35.370
of 18 months. Newton had been studying at
Cambridge University and had just

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:41.550
obtained his degree in 1665 when the
university had to close as a precaution

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:47.550
against the plague. So Newton returned
home to Woolsthorpe Manor and over the

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:52.350
next two years there developed his
theories on calculus, optics and

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:59.460
gravitation. It is at this home where the
now famous apple tree is located. 1666

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:06.180
was Newton's Year of Wonders, he was
aged 23 at the time and he later said

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:11.790
that "in those days I was in the prime of
my age for invention and minded

00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:17.670
mathematics and philosophy more than at
any time since". In this video I would

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:22.830
just like to focus on the work Newton
did during this time on the topic of

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:28.290
calculus and these pages are printouts
from the Cambridge University digital

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:32.369
library so the links for you to see the
originals yourself will be in the

00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:38.909
description. This first document written
by Newton and dated October 1666 has

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:45.570
come to be called the 1666 Tract on
Fluxions. It is the first collection of

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:51.329
Newton's ideas on calculus. It is dated
in a different ink so this date could

00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:56.520
have been added later on and there was
quite a rivalry between Newton and

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:02.490
Leibniz over who first described
calculus but regardless this document is

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:09.060
a collection of Newton's ideas since
1665 which can also be seen scattered

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:12.770
through his
earlier notebooks. It says to resolve

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:18.650
problems by motion these following
propositions are sufficient. He then lays

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:25.400
out a bunch of propositions and does
some examples. To Newton calculus was all

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:30.260
about motion and he was trying to
understand motion because the physics

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:35.780
problems he was also working on required
some kind of mathematical base such as

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:41.690
for gravitation. Neither Newton nor Leibniz were the first to completely come

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:44.930
up with calculus
they were both building upon the work

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:50.450
done by earlier mathematicians such as
Descartes. Let's work through this

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:55.820
demonstration here ourselves to see what
was going on. We're going to think about

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:02.060
the motion of a moving particle so at
one moment in time we could describe the

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:11.180
position of the particle with an x and a
y. These coordinates Newton would later

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:17.990
go on to call fluents
as they are flowing quantities. What

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:23.780
we want to know is how we would describe
this particle after a small period of

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:35.300
time. So if it has moved to here we would
describe its X position as being X plus

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:43.310
some new quantity and likewise in the Y
direction. To find how much it has moved

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:50.420
we would find the velocity of the
particle and multiply it by the small

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:54.710
change in time.
Newton refers to velocities in two

00:03:54.710 --> 00:04:03.410
directions as being P and Q and he uses
O to denote a very small infinitesimal

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:11.870
change in time, so in the X direction we
would write this as P times O. O is not

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:19.549
equal to zero but it is very small so
after this change in time our X has gone

00:04:19.549 --> 00:04:28.240
to X plus PO and our Y has gone to y
plus QO.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:36.770
Instead of using P and Q Newton would
later go on to use X dot and Y dot as

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:43.820
the velocities and he would call these
the fluxions but that would have to wait

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:51.290
until a 1671 rewrite of this work. We can
see it in Newton's notes here he says "if

00:04:51.290 --> 00:05:01.910
the described lines be X and Y in one
moment they will be X + PO and Y + QO in

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:08.030
the next. Newton then does a demonstration
where the relation between lines X and Y

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:16.729
is X cubed minus A B X plus A cubed
minus D Y squared equals zero. He says "I

00:05:16.729 --> 00:05:26.450
may substitute X plus PO and Y + QO into
the places of X + Y." To expand something

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:30.560
like this he would have used the
binomial expansion theorem which he also

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:36.320
had a hand in developing. I will denote
these zeros here with a line through

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:41.090
them to make sure that they aren't
confused with these O's in here which

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:44.810
are not equal to zero.
Newton then writes out the result of

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:51.200
this expansion and he says that since we
know X cubed minus ADX plus A cubed

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:57.500
minus D Y squared was zero we can find
those terms in our expansion and cancel

00:05:57.500 --> 00:06:03.320
them out and then he writes the result
of doing that. The next step is to divide

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:09.740
every term by O and were able to do
that since O is never actually equal to

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:16.520
zero and this is what we get. Newton then
says "also those terms are infinitely

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:22.520
little in which O is, therefore omitting
them there rests" and he gives the

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:26.580
solution. So if we cancel all of our
terms with an O in it as

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:31.830
being so small that they're not going to
contribute then we get the same solution

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:37.530
that Newton gets and it is our time
derivative of what we started with.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:43.340
Remember that this is a derivative with
respect to time so it's like we had

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:51.710
differentiated this implicitly. X cubed
has become 3X squared times P which is

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:58.949
dx/dt. That is exactly what you would get
differentiating this and taking into

00:06:58.949 --> 00:07:04.800
account that X and Y are functions of T.
This technique was a little

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:12.240
controversial because O is treated both
as being not zero and close enough to

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:18.240
zero to cancel out and nowadays we use
the notation of limits to make it more

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:25.259
rigorous. We would say that in the limit
of O going towards zero this term would

00:07:25.259 --> 00:07:29.639
go towards zero. Now this whole
demonstration here was actually a

00:07:29.639 --> 00:07:34.500
demonstration of proposition seven so
why don't we have a look back at

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:39.569
proposition seven to see what it was.
Proposition seven starts here and it

00:07:39.569 --> 00:07:43.620
talks about "having an equation
expressing the relation between two or

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:51.389
more lines X,Y and Z and the relation of
their velocities P, Q and R may be found

00:07:51.389 --> 00:07:57.270
by putting all the terms on one side of
the equation so that they are equal to

00:07:57.270 --> 00:08:05.879
nothing and first multiply each term by
how many times P over X as X have

00:08:05.879 --> 00:08:11.009
dimensions in the terms." Let's work
through what he's doing here. We're going

00:08:11.009 --> 00:08:15.029
to start with the same equation that we
had before and we'll find its derivative

00:08:15.029 --> 00:08:21.839
this way which is the same as saying the
relation of the velocities. So we times

00:08:21.839 --> 00:08:28.080
each term by P over X for how many
dimensions of X it has so for example

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:34.709
this first term has three dimensions of
X so we will do X cubed times three

00:08:34.709 --> 00:08:43.189
times P/X. The second term has one dimension of X.

00:08:45.199 --> 00:08:50.279
The third and fourth terms have zero
dimensions of X so we times it by

00:08:50.279 --> 00:08:57.180
zero times P over X which is the same as
multiplying it by zero so I'm not going

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:03.899
to write it down. He says that "secondly,
multiply each term by how many times Q

00:09:03.899 --> 00:09:10.769
over Y as Y has dimension in it." So we do
the same thing now for Y. The first three

00:09:10.769 --> 00:09:16.290
terms have zero dimension of Y so they
would be multiplied by zero but this

00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:28.319
last term has two dimensions of Y so he
would times it by two times Q over Y. If

00:09:28.319 --> 00:09:31.170
you had a third variable you would keep
going.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:37.709
He says the sum of all of these products
shall be equal to nothing, yep so it's

00:09:37.709 --> 00:09:44.160
equal to 0, and the equation gives the
relation of the velocities. So if we tidy

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:50.480
this equation up this X will cancel with
one of the X's up there and we will get

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:59.610
3X squared times P. These X's here will
cancel we'll get A B P. One of the Y's

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:09.000
will cancel we'll get minus 2 D Y Q
equals to zero and indeed this is the

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:14.160
time derivative of what we started with.
It was a quicker method than the one

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:18.600
we just did before but it's the same
result. I find that really awesome that

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:22.829
we were able to actually follow along
with Newton as he's doing some

00:10:22.829 --> 00:10:28.110
derivatives. We can see at the end
here that he gives us a general form for

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:34.769
doing this. Later in the document he goes
on to apply these theorems to resolving

00:10:34.769 --> 00:10:41.009
of problems you can see here he's
drawing tangents to crooked lines and

00:10:41.009 --> 00:10:47.309
over here, problem five is to find the
nature of the crooked line whose area is

00:10:47.309 --> 00:10:53.310
expressed by any given equation.
That is the nature of the area being

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:59.100
given to find the nature of the crooked
line whose area it is. All this talk

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:05.790
of area might remind you of integration
and Newton does go on to really talk

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:11.220
about the link between differentiation
and integration and finding the area

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:15.300
beneath a curve.
He seems aware that these two things are

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:21.360
inverses and that is the fundamental
theorem of calculus. This is another

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:25.200
document written by Newton but at a
later time and I just wanted to show it

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:29.580
to you because it shows that he does
later go on to use the terminology

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:36.150
fluxions where instead of using P and Q
for the velocities he uses X dot and Y

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:41.310
dot but the rest of the examples here
are the same. Fluxions were kind of

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:46.590
central to the whole Leibniz-Newton
controversy and in fact the last

00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:52.590
document I would like to show you is a
letter in Latin that Newton wrote to

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:59.030
Leibniz via another middle man called
Henry Oldenburg and this was dated the

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:06.420
24th of October 1676
and in it Newton explains fluxions but

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:12.300
actually conceals his words in code
because he was so suspicious of Leibniz.

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:17.970
Around here he says "I cannot proceed
with the explanation of the fluxions now,

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:25.250
I have preferred to conceal it thus" and
then he puts this random string of

00:12:25.250 --> 00:12:30.960
numbers and letters and it looks a bit
like a Bitcoin address but actually it's

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:37.770
an enciphered phrase and this phrase here
defines the relationship between the

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:42.030
fluent and fluxion.
Now what he did to get this, was he took

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:48.780
the phrase in Latin saying "given an
equation that consists of any number of

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:54.930
flowing quantities to find the flexions
and vice-versa" and he counted the

00:12:54.930 --> 00:13:00.390
frequency of each letter and ordered
them alphabetically. If there were three

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:03.330
or more
of a letter then he would put a number

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:10.050
in front so it looks like there were six
A's and nine N's. Even if Leibniz could

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:14.850
decode this, the phrase doesn't seem to
show much, although it must have given

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:20.160
Newton some kind of security over the
idea. The fact he could put it down on

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:26.250
paper and make a claim in this fight
about his ideas being stolen. This issue

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:31.950
of ownership became so complicated
because Newton's work on fluxions and

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:37.230
calculus and many other things wasn't
published until a long time after he

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:42.270
wrote it. Even Leibniz's work wasn't
published straight away. I thought

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:46.500
this little document here would be a
nice insight into the relationship

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:51.960
between the two men. So that's been a
look at some of Newton's original work

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:56.730
even as a math student I don't think I
had really seen much of his original

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:01.320
thinking so I hope you found this video
a little bit interesting. You can go to

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:05.520
the links in the description to the
Cambridge University digital library to

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:10.350
see these documents as well as many more
about Newton. This video was made

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:15.270
possible by my viewers who support me on
patreon so if you'd like to help me

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:20.040
continue making videos like this then
please consider supporting me there too.

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:27.450
It's patreon.com/Tibees.
Thank you to my current patrons and a

